# --- Local harvest scratch ---
# Raw responses are line-by-line replays of third-party pages. They are useful while debugging a
# site locally but must never be committed -- this is the one category that is genuine copied
# content rather than a derived index.
data/raw/
data/normalized/
data/reports/
data/reports/*.local.*

# --- Generated artefacts: what IS committed, and why ---
# The subscription index and the catalogue shards ARE committed, because the whole point of the
# project is a jsDelivr-servable subscription URL:
#
#     https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/<owner>/<repo>@main/data/tvbox/index.json
#
# That URL can only resolve if the file is in the repository. What gets published is an index of
# *addresses* -- site keys, category names, titles, play URLs -- derived from catalogues the
# operator explicitly enabled. No page content, no media, and no raw responses are published;
# every generated file is rebuilt from scratch on each run, so the repository never accumulates
# history of a source the operator has since disabled.
#
# `data/raw/`, `data/normalized/` and `data/reports/` are excluded above: the first is copied
# content, the second is a debugging intermediate, and the third is operational telemetry that
# has no reason to live in git history.

# --- Workflow scratch ---
.ci/
*.local.yaml

